<section className="faq-container">
  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>What is a digital marketing course and what does it include?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> A digital marketing course teaches how to promote businesses online. It includes SEO, social media marketing, Google Ads, content marketing, email marketing, and basic analytics to help brands grow on digital platforms.</p>
  </details>

  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>Who should join a digital marketing training program?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> Anyone can join a digital marketing training program, including students, freshers, working professionals, business owners, and freelancers. No technical background or coding knowledge is required to start learning digital marketing.</p>
  </details>

  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>What digital marketing jobs are available after completing a course?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> After completing a digital marketing course, you can apply for jobs like digital marketing executive, SEO executive, social media manager, PPC specialist, content marketer, or email marketing executive.</p>
  </details>

  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>Is digital marketing an IT job or a non-technical career?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> Digital marketing is mostly a non-technical career. It focuses on marketing skills, creativity, and strategy. Basic tools are used, but coding or an IT background is not required.</p>
  </details>

  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>Is digital marketing a good long-term career in India?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> Yes, digital marketing is a good long-term career in India. As businesses move online, the demand for skilled digital marketers continues to grow across industries.</p>
  </details>

  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>What is the average digital marketing salary in India for freshers?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> The average digital marketing salary in India for freshers ranges from ₹2.5 LPA to ₹5 LPA. Salary depends on skills, practical experience, and knowledge of tools like SEO and paid ads.</p>
  </details>

  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>What are the main types of digital marketing I will learn in a course?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> In a digital marketing course, you usually learn SEO, social media marketing, Google Ads, content marketing, email marketing, affiliate marketing, and basic analytics.</p>
  </details>

  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>What is a digital marketing course with AI and how is it useful?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> A digital marketing course with AI teaches how to use AI tools for content creation, ad optimization, audience targeting, and data analysis. AI helps marketers work faster and make better decisions.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>Which digital marketing course offers placement support in India?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> Many digital marketing courses in India offer placement support such as resume help, interview preparation, and job assistance to help students start their careers after course completion.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>How do I choose the best digital marketing institute for learning?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> To choose the best digital marketing institute, check the course syllabus, practical training, trainer experience, tools covered, student reviews, and placement support offered.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>What should I check before joining a digital marketing institute in Delhi?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> Before joining a digital marketing institute in Delhi, check course duration, practical projects, batch size, placement support, and whether the training is updated with current industry tools.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details className="faq slide-up-section">
    <summary>Can beginners start a digital marketing course without prior experience?</summary>
    <p><span style={{"color":"#00a2ff"}}>Answer:</span> Yes, beginners can start a digital marketing course without any prior experience. Most courses are designed from basic to advanced levels and are suitable for non-technical learners.</p>
  </details>
  
  
</section>



